"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-760f2e194e5aa459410b663a","relation":{"from":"reliable enough","relation":"depends_on","to":"load"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-9cde998ad5c9f298bc8e55e7","relation":{"from":"battery bank","relation":"part_of","to":"power supply setup"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-b67d2882420c9206a2e3d2aa","relation":{"from":"solar panel with a battery bank","relation":"supports","to":"essentials"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"020f417e-a6e6-46e2-a38b-88d13ecea5ba","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"49443ae9-1984-4149-a551-791db43f82d1","source_slot":"s1"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"020f417e-a6e6-46e2-a38b-88d13ecea5ba","text":"You have spoken with this conversational partner before. Earlier conversations involved gardening and planning a trip. I am setting up a remote workshop with limited equipment and infrequent deliveries. What should remain usable if one part fails?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"49443ae9-1984-4149-a551-791db43f82d1","text":"Since you're planning a remote workshop with limited equipment and infrequent deliveries, it sounds like a high-risk setup! If one part fails, you need to prioritize redundancy and robustness.\n\nWhat exactly are you planning? Knowing what kind of equipment or specific part you're worried about failing will help me give you the best advice on what to keep on hand or what's essential for the rest of the project."},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s2","source_id":"4d9563ac-4422-4c87-840e-f59db313b7a0","text":"I was thinking about the power supply setup. If the main generator fails, I need something that can keep the essentials running. Do you think a solar panel with a battery bank would be reliable enough?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"23d47004-31f4-4c80-960f-e0654598f391","text":"A solar panel with a battery bank is a very solid concept for a remote setup, especially if power reliability is critical.\n\nHowever, \"reliable enough\" really depends on the *load*. What are you planning to run? Is it a small, low-draw setup like a few lights and a small computer, or is it a full, high-power workshop setup?\n\nIf your \"essentials\" include a high-power tool or machinery, the battery bank will need to be significantly larger to handle peak loads.\n\nTo give you the best advice, could you tell me what specific \"essentials\" or \"parts\" are most critical? For instance, are you running servers, specialized machinery, or just basic lighting and communication?\""}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":[],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-6cd26eb86712f4ac34d11b07","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":[],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},"evidence":{"end":462,"quote":"If your \"essentials\" include a high-power tool or machinery, the battery bank will need to be significantly larger to handle peak loads.","source_slot":"s3","start":326},"expression_status":"unknown","monitor_id":"candidate:e-6